# The Affair at Bramblefen — a one-shot scenario bundling three maps.
#
# Demonstrates the `scenario { ... }` block: scenario-level boxed text
# (read-aloud), DM notes (private), and a sequence of `map "path"`
# references. Render with:
#
#     uv run dmap render-scenario samples/bramblefen_affair.dmap \
#       -o bramblefen.html
#
# The output is a self-contained HTML document — one section per map,
# print-ready (each map breaks onto its own page).

scenario "The Affair at Bramblefen" {
  description """
  The trail of stolen cattle ends at a crack in the hillside above
  Bramblefen Crossing. Locals say bones hang on twine from low branches
  outside the cleft — fox skulls, mostly, but one or two too long for
  any fox. Captain Reswick will pay 50 gp a head for the cattle's
  return, and another 50 if the raiders are dealt with.
  """
  dm_notes """
  Three-session scope. The party arrives at Bramblefen Crossing
  (overland map) and questions Headwoman Merryn. She points them at
  the goblin warren in the West Wood — but quietly. She will not
  speak openly against the standing-stones fey court.

  Pace:
    • Session 1 — Bramblefen Crossing. Roleplay, optional fey hook
      at the standing stones.
    • Session 2 — Goblin Warren. Combat-heavy. Broken Tooth may flee
      if reduced below 8 HP — leaves a "Goblin reprisal" clock.
    • Session 3 — Crypt of Saint Vellis. A side hook: the ritualist
      from the throne chamber was hired by the same patron as the
      goblins. Resolve or escalate.

  Faction reactions to a full clear:
    • Bramblefen — Merryn cordial; free room and board for one night.
    • Standing-stones court — neutral if PCs left the ring alone;
      hostile clock if they took anything from the centre pillar.
  """

  map "overland.dmap"
  map "goblin_warren.dmap"
  map "crypt.dmap"
}
